# Champion genomes and populations for the reported runs (experiment 01's seven, and 01b) ARE committed: they are small
# (about 2 MB in total) and they make the results checkable -- anyone can re-run the ablation or
# the tactics measurement against the exact strains. Everything else under runs/ is regenerable.
!runs/m4/champion-*.npz
!runs/m8/champion-*.npz
!runs/m9-calibrated/champion-*.npz
!runs/m9-uncalibrated/champion-*.npz
!runs/m7/*.npz
!runs/m7-varied/*.npz
!runs/exp01b-direction-corrected/champion-*.npz

# The frozen opponent suite is NEVER committed. It is an unevolved population, so its weights are
# proportional to the connectome's anatomical weights (measured: 100% of entries), and this project
# does not redistribute that data. It regenerates deterministically from its seed.
*frozen-suite*.npz

# --- reviewer workspaces and tool attachments: local, not part of the published record ---
# Astra 6's review workspace (its own AGENTS.md, reviews, proposals) and files attached to Codex
# sessions. Findings that change the project are recorded in DECISIONS.md, not here.
Astra6/
.codex-remote-attachments/

# --- agent working files (plan ledgers) ---
.superpowers/
